flowchart TD
    start([Start or resume project]) --> restore[Validate index, workflow version, records and evidence]
%% @airflow-context restore
%% Initialize missing .air/ using the global instructions. On resume,
%% validate the saved node and call stack, then continue that exact pending step;
%% the entry decision below is for runs without an active saved position.
%% Do not replay Concept or choose a phase from artifact existence alone.
%%
%% # Workflow revision: explicit orchestration and self-review
%%
%% This revision changes transition semantics. Existing runs must follow the global instructions'
%% Resume validation rules and receive user authorization before changing versions.
%% Retain the old source and call stack until the pending work is reconciled.
%%
%% - Old position; New position / required reconciliation
%% - Project start -> concept; restore; validate saved position or current Concept approval
%% - Verification implementation; Project implementation; preserve target and repair findings
%% - Verification definition; Project definition; preserve target and proposed change
%% - Verification releasePlanning; Project releasePlanning; preserve impact and decision evidence
%% - Verification design / designForChangedDefinition; Project design; preserve required reapproval
%% - Verification impact / scopeImpact / designImpact; Corresponding Project node; preserve impact evidence
%% - Verification moreUnverified; Project select; inspect current feature evidence
%% - Verification releaseDiagnosis / releaseRootCause; Verification diagnosis / rootCause in release mode
%% - Verification testing / featureChecksPassed; Same node in feature mode; add explicit target
%% - Verification releaseChecks / releaseChecksPassed; Same node in release mode; validate feature evidence
%% - Implementation start / plan; Same node with explicit feature ID and new-work/rework mode
%% - Design review; Same node, followed by mandatory quality decision
%% - Definition specify; Same node, followed by mandatory self-review
%% - Project releaseApproval / awaitingPublication; Same node; successful authorization leads to publish
%%
%% Other retained IDs do not by themselves establish semantic compatibility. Remove
%% obsolete nested repair frames only after reconciling their pending outcome with
%% Project. Never infer approval or publication success from migration. Re-evaluate
%% only evidence affected by changed criteria; block when mapping is ambiguous.
%%
%% ## Status ownership revision
%%
%% Split legacy combined inventory status columns into Records (`record_status`),
%% Features (`feature_status`) and Releases (`release_status`). Keep content files
%% free of mutable statuses. Migrate one release status per version from evidence;
%% never interpret Design `approved` as release `published` or record approval as
%% release lifecycle. Preserve historical events. Conflicting legacy statuses require
%% reconciliation before resuming. Apply the global instructions' user-authorized version
%% migration rules; do not silently migrate an active run.
%%
%% Workflow maintenance checks: new project; next release; nested resume; rejected
%% Design; changed Definition; code/design defects; missing evidence or tracker
%% conflict; workflow migration; verified feature repair; Design revision with reuse;
%% removed, deferred and cancelled scope. Trace these before publishing method changes.
%% @end-airflow-context
    restore --> resume{Valid saved position?}
    resume -- Yes --> saved([Resume validated node and call stack])
    resume -- Inconsistent --> blocked([Blocked: report evidence and required decision])
    resume -- No active position --> conceptNeeded{Current Concept approval valid?}
    conceptNeeded -- No --> concept[["Concept: concept.mmd"]]
    conceptNeeded -- Yes --> featureIntake[["Feature intake: feature-intake.mmd"]]
    concept -- Concept approved --> featureIntake
    featureIntake -- Approved backlog ready --> releasePlanning[["Release planning: release-planning.mmd"]]
    featureIntake -- Blocked --> blocked
    featureIntake -- No approved features --> projectIdle([Project idle])
    releasePlanning -- Scope approved --> design[["Design: design.mmd"]]
    releasePlanning -- Planning deferred --> projectIdle
    releasePlanning -- Release cancelled --> projectIdle
    design -- Design approved --> select[Select next scoped feature needing implementation or verification]
    design -- Release deferred or cancelled --> projectIdle
    design -- Blocked --> blocked
    select --> work{Pending work?}
    work -- Implementation needed --> implementation[["Implementation: implementation.mmd"]]
    work -- Feature verification needed --> verification[["Verification: verification.mmd"]]
    work -- All scoped features verified: release mode --> verification
%% @airflow-context select
%% On entry after Design approval, transition release design-approved -> implementing
%% once current Definition/scope/Design approvals are valid. This status covers
%% feature implementation, reuse assessment and feature verification, even when
%% no code changes are needed. The AI records the transition from evidence here,
%% not inside Implementation. Release Verification alone moves implementing -> verifying.
%% Apply the responsible phase transition rules before selecting work.
%% Use current evidence and dependency ordering; preserve unaffected feature work.
%% Pass feature ID, new-work/rework mode and findings to Implementation. Pass
%% feature/release mode and target IDs to Verification. Record caller and next
%% action in the index. Never select a new feature while current rework is pending.
%%
%% Feature transitions owned by this phase:
%% - `implementing` / `verifying` / `verified` -> `selected`: Scope or Design approval invalidated, with Definition unchanged; wait for renewed approvals before repair or reuse.
%% - `verified` -> `released`: Containing release publication is confirmed and authorized.
%% - Active status -> `blocked`: Unresolved conflict or external blocker; save prior status and required resolution.
%% - `blocked` -> Saved prior status: Cause resolved and prior status invariants still hold; otherwise apply the relevant revision transition from that saved status.
%%
%% ## Subflow calls and outcomes
%%
%% Project owns feature selection and cross-phase repair routing. Verification takes
%% `feature` or `release` mode and returns evidence-backed outcomes. Implementation
%% receives a feature ID, `new-work` or `rework` mode and findings; it returns to its
%% actual caller without changing target. Store these arguments with the call frame.
%% For multiple affected features, record the pending target IDs and process them in
%% dependency order. Invalidate affected verification before selection; preserve
%% unaffected evidence with an impact rationale. Run release checks only when every
%% scoped feature has current passing evidence.
%% @end-airflow-context
    implementation -- Feature ready: feature mode --> verification
    implementation -- Blocked --> blocked
    verification -- Feature passed --> select
    verification -- Implementation defect: same target and findings --> implementation
    verification -- Design gap --> design
    verification -- Definition change --> definition[["Definition: definition.mmd"]]
    verification -- Blocked --> blocked
    definition -- Revised and approved --> impact[Assess changed Definition impact and invalidate affected evidence]
    definition -- Deferred or rejected --> releasePlanning
    definition -- Blocked --> blocked
    impact --> scopeImpact{Scope approval affected?}
    scopeImpact -- Yes --> releasePlanning
    scopeImpact -- No --> designImpact{Design approval affected?}
    designImpact -- Yes --> design
    designImpact -- No --> select
%% @airflow-context impact
%% Apply the impact rules below. Preserve unaffected evidence
%% only with an explicit impact rationale. If impact cannot be bounded, block.
%%
%% ### Release revision and repair transitions
%%
%% Normal release lifecycle: planning -> scope-pending-approval -> scope-approved
%% -> design-pending-approval -> design-approved -> implementing -> verifying
%% -> release-ready -> pending-publication-authorization -> published.
%% All except published are active. Deferred, blocked and cancelled are exceptions.
%% Initial status is `planning`. Apply the earliest affected prerequisite first:
%%
%% - From; To; Required condition and evidence
%% - Any active status after `planning`; `planning`; Scope approval invalidated: revise scope draft, then request approval through the normal route. Invalidate dependent Design and release checks.
%% - `design-pending-approval` / `design-approved` / `implementing` / `verifying` / `release-ready` / `pending-publication-authorization`; `scope-approved`; Scope remains approved but Design approval is invalidated; revise Design draft, then request its approval.
%% - `verifying` / `release-ready` / `pending-publication-authorization`; `implementing`; Approvals remain valid; affected feature implementation or feature checks need work.
%% - `release-ready` / `pending-publication-authorization`; `verifying`; All feature evidence remains valid; repeat release-level checks only.
%% - `scope-pending-approval`; `planning`; Human requests scope revision; scope record returns to `draft`.
%% - `design-pending-approval`; `scope-approved`; Human requests Design revision; Design record returns to `draft`.
%%
%% A Definition revision pauses affected work at `clarifying` and triggers impact
%% analysis. If scope approval is affected, use `planning`; if only Design approval
%% is affected, use `scope-approved`; otherwise use `implementing` for affected
%% feature work. An already earlier release status stays there. Re-entering
%% implementation never bypasses approval checks for the revised Definition.
%%
%% Every revision after release checks invalidates affected checks and publication
%% authorization. Re-request authorization after required checks pass. Authorization
%% also binds the exact code/build being published, not just scope and Design files.
%% A user-requested repeat check suspends publication until it passes; if inputs are
%% unchanged, previously recorded authorization may remain valid with evidence.
%%
%% For `blocked`, save the prior status and apply revision rules to that status before
%% resuming. For `deferred`, retain the hold; changes may invalidate evidence but do
%% not resume work. Explicit reopening enters `planning` and revalidates scope.
%% `published` and `cancelled` are terminal: use a new release version for later work.
%% Changing a version retires the old unpublished release through explicit cancellation
%% and creates a new planning entry; never silently rename a release ID.
%%
%% - Change; Approval/evidence impact; Resume point
%% - Project purpose, users, outcome or boundary; Concept approval becomes stale; assess dependencies and mark only affected feature definitions, scopes and designs for reapproval.; Concept approval, then affected records; preserve unaffected approvals with evidence.
%% - Feature behavior, scope, non-goals, dependencies or acceptance criteria; Definition approval becomes stale. Use dependency impact analysis to mark only affected scope/design approvals and feature verification stale; preserve unaffected approvals with evidence.; Definition; then reapprove only affected scope/design before continuing.
%% - Release feature set, version, exclusions or goals; Scope approval and integrated design approval become stale; release-level verification becomes stale.; Release planning.
%% - Integrated design architecture, interface, data flow or constraints; Design approval becomes stale; implementation and verification evidence for impacted features becomes stale.; Design approval, then reimplement/reverify impacted features.
%% - Implementation code or configuration; Design/definition approval remains only if inputs are unchanged; checks covering changed behavior become stale.; Implementation checks and affected feature verification; rerun release integration checks for shared behavior.
%% @end-airflow-context
    impact -- Unclear impact --> blocked
    verification -- Release passed --> releaseApproval{Human authorizes publication?}
    releaseApproval -- No decision --> awaitingPublication([Awaiting publication authorization])
    releaseApproval -- Yes --> publish[Publish authorized release]
    awaitingPublication -- Authorization received --> publish
    awaitingPublication -- Additional checks: release mode --> verification
    awaitingPublication -- Release cancelled --> projectIdle
    publish --> published{Publication confirmed?}
    published -- Yes --> releasePublished([Release published])
    published -- Failed or unknown --> blocked
%% @airflow-context publish
%% Revalidate scope/Design approvals, all required checks and explicit publication
%% authorization against the exact release. Execute only permitted publication
%% actions. Record published status only with success evidence. On failure or an
%% uncertain result, inspect actual deployment state before any retry; never
%% assume success or repeat a potentially completed side effect blindly.
%% @end-airflow-context
    releasePublished --> anotherRelease{Plan another release now?}
    anotherRelease -- Yes --> featureIntake
    anotherRelease -- No --> projectIdle
    projectIdle -- User requests new feature or release --> featureIntake

    classDef boundary fill:#126a52,color:#ffffff,stroke:#126a52
    classDef approval fill:#fff0e8,color:#633b2c,stroke:#c68162
    class start,saved,blocked,projectIdle,awaitingPublication,releasePublished boundary
    class releaseApproval,anotherRelease approval

%% @airflow-context releaseApproval
%% Release transition `release-ready -> pending-publication-authorization`: Record check results and request publication authorization for current scope/design digests. Owner: AI requests; human decides.
%%
%% Release transition `pending-publication-authorization -> published`: Explicit authorization matches the current release digests; publication action is permitted and its success is confirmed. Owner: Human authorizes; AI executes only if permitted.
%%
%% Release transition Any active release -> `blocked`: An unresolved conflict, unavailable required evidence or external blocker prevents progress. Diagnosed failures use the impact node repair transitions. Owner: AI records; resolution may require human input.
%%
%% Release transition `blocked -> prior active status`: Cause resolved and prior invariants hold; otherwise apply the applicable repair transition from the saved status. Owner: AI based on evidence; human for approval transitions.
%%
%% Release transition Pre-publication status -> `deferred` / `cancelled`: User explicitly defers or cancels the release. Owner: Human.
%% @end-airflow-context
